@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — The five destinations at every viewport band
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Member" as actor
box "Frontend — Barnabas web" #E0F2FE
  participant "ViewportService" as vp
  participant "AppShellComponent" as shell
  participant "PrimaryNavComponent" as primary
  participant "BottomNavComponent" as bottom
  participant "NavDestinations" as nav
end box

actor -> shell : Open any screen
shell -> vp : Read the current band
alt band is Medium or wider
  vp --> shell : Medium, Large, or ExtraLarge
  shell -> primary : Render with the destinations and the current one
  primary -> nav : Read the ordered list
  nav --> primary : Board, Search, Post, Inbox, You
  primary --> actor : Five destinations in the header
else band is ExtraSmall or Small
  vp --> shell : ExtraSmall or Small
  shell -> bottom : Render with the destinations and the current one
  bottom -> nav : Read the same ordered list
  nav --> bottom : Board, Search, Post, Inbox, You
  bottom --> actor : The same five, in the same order, in the bottom bar
end
note over nav : L2-109 is satisfied structurally: both navigations\nread one list, so a destination cannot exist at\none band and be missing at another.
@enduml
